[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mTeamFortressMap Specification[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mApart from being a normal map, TeamFortress Maps[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mhave the following changes:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32mAuto Detection[m
[32m+[m	[32mTeam SpawnPoints[m
[32m+[m	[32mArmor[m[41m 				 [m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32mGoals[m
[32m+[m	[32mGoalItems[m
[32m+[m	[32mTimer Goals[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf you are only interested in the changes made to the map specs[m
[32m+[m[32msince the last version, to update your maps etc, then check[m
[32m+[m[32mout the section entitled "Summary of Changes"[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mNotes about using existing Entities[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mIn TeamFortress, we have an Observer mode, where players who haven't[m
[32m+[m[32mchosen a class, or have run out of lives, are able to cycle through[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mall the Intermission points to watch the action.[m
[32m+[m[32mBecause of this, make sure you have a few Intermission points at[m
[32m+[m[32minteresting viewing locations around the map. If you don't have some[m
[32m+[m[32mof these, Observers won't have much fun.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mAuto Detection[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mTeamFortress maps will be automatically detected by the TeamFortress patch[m
[32m+[m[32mif you put an entity in the map with a classname of "info_tfdetect".[m
[32m+[m[32mThis makes TeamFortress automatically turn on the FORTRESSMAP toggleflag,[m
[32m+[m[32mand turn on teamplay.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAlso, once the TeamFortress map has been detected, the patch will look[m
[32m+[m[32mfor any spawnpoints dedicated to teams (see below).[m
[32m+[m[32mIf it finds any, it will look for the highest team number that is used.[m
[32m+[m[32mOnce found, it will limit anybody attempting to join a team to that[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mnumber.[m
[32m+[m[32mAt the moment, Maps are limited to a maximum of 4 teams.[m
[32m+[m[32mE.g. If the highest team number used by a Team Spawnpoint is 3, then[m
[32m+[m	[32m the patch will only allow players to join teams 1, 2, and 3.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe detection entity can also do the following:[m
[32m+[m	[32m- specify a version string in the "broadcast" variable.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  This will be compared with the version string for the TeamFortress[m
[32m+[m	[32m  patch. If the don't match, a warning will be displayed to the[m
[32m+[m	[32m  player that their patch and the map are incompatible.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  The version string is in the format as follows:[m
[32m+[m		[32mTeamFortress v2.1[m
[32m+[m	[32m  The string is case sensitive, so make sure you've got it right.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  Don't put a \n on the end of it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Set the state of the toggleflags when the map starts up. The[m
[32m+[m	[32m  value of the toggleflags should be in the "impulse" variable.[m
[32m+[m[32m          The bits for the toggleflags are:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    Bit 1 (1)   :   Off - ClasSkin              , On - Multiskin[m
[32m+[m[32m    Bit 2 (2)   :   Off - ClassPersistence Off  , On - ClassPersistence On[m
[32m+[m[32m    Bit 3 (4)   :   Off - CheatChecking Off     , On - CheatChecking On[m
[32m+[m[32m    Bit 4 (8)   :   Off - FortressMap Off       , On - FortressMap On[m
[32m+[m[32m    Bit 5 (16)  :   Off - RespawnDelay Off      , On - RespawnDelay (See below)[m
[32m+[m[32m    Bit 6 (32)  :   Off - RespawnDelay Off      , On - RespawnDelay (See below)[m
[32m+[m[32m    Bit 7 (64)  :   Off - AutoTeam Off          , On - AutoTeam On[m
[32m+[m	[32mBit 8 (128)	:	Off - Individual Frags		, On - Frags = TeamScore[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m        N.B. FortressMap will be set On automatically by the the[m
[32m+[m[32m             Detection entity anyway, so just ignore that Bit.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m		[32mN.B. The RespawnDelay settings takes 2 bits. The value of both of[m
[32m+[m			[32m them determines the level of respawn delay, as follows:[m
[32m+[m				[32mBit 5  		Bit 6		Result[m
[32m+[m				[32m Off		 Off		No Respawn delays[m
[32m+[m				[32m On			 Off		5 Second respawn delay[m
[32m+[m				[32m Off		 On			10 Second respawn delay[m
[32m+[m				[32m On			 On			20 Second respawn delay[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Specify a string which is then "localcmd"ed. This allows you[m
[32m+[m	[32m  to automatically set gravity, friction, etc.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  The string should be stored in the "message" variable.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Put a limit on the number of lives each player has. When a player[m
[32m+[m	[32m  runs out of lives, they are stuck in observer mode for the rest[m
[32m+[m	[32m  of the level.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  Lives for each player depend on the setting for the team they[m
[32m+[m	[32m  belong to. The number of lives players of each team be should[m
[32m+[m	[32m  be specified in the following variables:[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 1	:	"ammo_shells"[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 2	:	"ammo_nails"[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 3	:	"ammo_rockets"[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 4	:	"ammo_cells"[m
[32m+[m	[32m  If the value of any team is 0, then the players of that team get[m
[32m+[m	[32m  infinite lives.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Specify any playerclass that is _not_ allowed on this map[m
[32m+[m	[32m  for each particular team.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  The bits of the four variables are used for this.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  The variables are as follows:[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 1	:	"maxammo_shells"[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 2	:	"maxammo_nails"[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 3	:	"maxammo_rockets"[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 4	:	"maxammo_cells"[m
[32m+[m	[32m  Also, the "playerclass" variable can be used to restrict classes[m
[32m+[m	[32m  for all teams.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  The bits for all the variables are as follows:[m
[32m+[m[41m      [m	[32mBit 1 (1)	:   No Scout[m[41m            [m
[32m+[m[32m        Bit 2 (2)	:	No Sniper[m[41m        [m
[32m+[m[32m        Bit 3 (4)	:	No Soldier[m[41m       [m
[32m+[m[32m        Bit 4 (8)	:	No Demolitions Man[m
[32m+[m[32m        Bit 5 (16)	:	No Combat Medic[m
[32m+[m[32m        Bit 6 (32)	:	No Heavy Weapons Guy[m
[32m+[m[32m        Bit 7 (64)	:	No Pyro[m
[32m+[m[32m        Bit 8 (128)	:	No Random PlayerClass[m
[32m+[m		[32mBit 9 (256) :	No Spy[m
[32m+[m		[32mBit 10(512) :	No Engineer[m
[32m+[m	[32m  E.g. If the "maxammo_nails" variable is set to 3, then players[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m       in Team 2 will be unable to play Scouts or Snipers.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m  Finally, if you want the Team to be a special team for a fancy[m
[32m+[m	[32m  map, such as the President in President-Quake, then you can[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m  restrict the team to only play Civilian Class. Do this by setting[m
[32m+[m	[32m  the team's variable to "-1".[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mNotes:[m
[32m+[m	[32mWhen using the "message" variable to set do localcmd's, you[m
[32m+[m	[32mcan issue more than one command by seperating them with \n[m
[32m+[m	[32mMake sure you end it with a \n too.[m
[32m+[m	[32mE.g. The following changes the gravity and the friction.[m
[32m+[m		[32m"message" "sv_gravity 200\nsv_friction .5\n"[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mTeam Spawnpoints[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mThere is now a new entity for Team Spawnpoints. Team Spawnpoints are used[m
[32m+[m[32mto make players only spawn in points designated for their team. Use it[m
[32m+[m[32mto make players spawn inside their own base/fortress.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe entity is called "info_player_teamspawn", and the "team_no" variable[m
[32m+[m[32msets the team_no that owns this spawnpoint.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAlso, spawnpoints allow you to give any player the spawns from this[m
[32m+[m[32mpoint a GoalItem. This is done using the following variables:[m
[32m+[m	[32m"items"				:	Contains the ID of the GoalItem to give[m
[32m+[m	[32m"message"			:	Message displayed to anyone who spawns on this[m
[32m+[m							[32mpoint.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe "goal_activation" of the Spawnpoint determines how the above works:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m1	:	If set, then every player who spawns on this point[m
[32m+[m			[32mwill be given a copy of the GoalItem. Otherwise, only[m[41m [m
[32m+[m			[32mthe first player to spawn will be given it.[m
[32m+[m	[32m2	:	If set, then every player who spawns on this point[m
[32m+[m			[32mwill have the "message" displayed to them. Otherwise, only[m[41m [m
[32m+[m			[32mthe first player to spawn will be see it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAlso, the "goal_effects" variable of the spawnpoint sets the re-use[m
[32m+[m[32mbehaviour of the spawnpoint. If it's 1, then the spawnpoint removes[m
[32m+[m[32mitself after someone has spawned on it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mArmor[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mTeamFortress supports not only armor levels and absorption percentages the[m
[32m+[m[32msame way Quake does: it also supports armor classes. E.g. Armor can be designed[m
[32m+[m[32mto prevent particular attack types.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe Armor Types are as follows:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m		[32mKevlar		:		Better protection against Bullets[m
[32m+[m		[32mWooden ;)	:		Better protection against Nails[m
[32m+[m		[32mBlast		:		Better protection against Explosions[m
[32m+[m		[32mShock		:		Better protection against Electricity[m
[32m+[m		[32mCeramic		:		Better protection against Fire[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTo use these armor types, just create an armor entity on the map as usual,[m
[32m+[m[32mand set it's "armorclass" variable. The "armorclass" is used as bitfields,[m
[32m+[m[32mas follows:[m
[32m+[m[41m      [m	[32mBit 1 (1)	:   Kevlar[m
[32m+[m[32m        Bit 2 (2)	:	Wooden[m
[32m+[m[32m        Bit 3 (4)	:	Blast[m
[32m+[m[32m        Bit 4 (8)	:	Shock[m
[32m+[m[32m        Bit 5 (16)	:	Ceramic[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAny combination of armor is legal, but try not to have armor which[m
[32m+[m[32mis too good.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoal Summary / Terminology[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoals are the really fun things you can do with TeamFortressMaps.[m
[32m+[m[32mA goal is simply an entity you place in a map. It is then handled[m
[32m+[m[32min the game based on the flags you give it. They're essentially[m
[32m+[m[32mmore complex triggers. I've kept all the code separate from[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mthe triggers tho, to allow us to toggle the use of them ingame.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe flags and variables set for a Goal allow us to create powerful[m
[32m+[m[32mmaps without changing the QuakeC code at all.[m
[32m+[m[32m-----------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoals[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m-----------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoals are always in one of the following states:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mACTIVE	:	The goal has been activated in some way.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m			[32mIt cannot be touched by a player.[m
[32m+[m			[32mActive goals return to the INACTIVE state based on their[m
[32m+[m			[32mresult criteria, or when they're forced into INACTIVE state[m
[32m+[m			[32mby another goal.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mINACTIVE:	The goal is not active.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m			[32mIt can be activated by players, and if the players meet the[m[41m [m
[32m+[m			[32mactivation criteria, the goal moves	to the ACTIVE state.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mREMOVED :	The goal is not active.[m
[32m+[m			[32mIt cannot be touched by players.[m
[32m+[m			[32mRemoved goals can still be activated by other goals, in which[m
[32m+[m			[32mcase they move to the ACTIVE state.[m
[32m+[m			[32mRemoved goals can be restored to the INACTIVE by being restored[m
[32m+[m			[32mby another goal.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTerminology[m
[32m+[m[32m-----------[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mactivated	: Goal moves to the ACTIVE state[m
[32m+[m[32minactivate	: If the Goal is in ACTIVE state, it moves to the INACTIVE state[m
[32m+[m[32mremoved		: Goal moves to the REMOVED state[m
[32m+[m[32mrestored	: If the Goal is in REMOVED state, it moves to the INACTIVE state[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mreturned	: GoalItems can be returned to their starting point, based on[m
[32m+[m			[32m  a number of settings.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGoal Group  : A group of goals that can be altered as one.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mActivating Player(AP): The player who either touched the Goal, or set the[m
[32m+[m					[32m   detpack which touched the Goal. In the case of GoalItems,[m
[32m+[m					[32m   the player that's attempting to pick up the GoalItem.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mActions[m
[32m+[m[32m-------[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen goals go to ACTIVE state, they can perform various actions.[m
[32m+[m[32mThese include:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Increase the score of the team the AP belongs to.[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Display a message to all players[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Display a message just to the AP[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Alter the details of one or more players, as follows:[m
[32m+[m		[32m- Give the player extra lives (if applicable)[m
[32m+[m		[32m- Alter a player's health/ammo/armor/powerups[m
[32m+[m		[32m- Give the player(s) a GoalItem[m
[32m+[m		[32m- Remove a GoalItem from the player(s)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m		[32mThe player can be the AP, all the members of a Team the AP is/isn't in,[m
[32m+[m		[32mall the players on the map, everyone but the AP, all the players[m[41m [m
[32m+[m		[32mwithin a specified distance from the goal, or everyone in/not in one[m[41m [m
[32m+[m		[32mparticular team.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activate another goal, applying the bonuses of the goal to the AP[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activate another goal, without applying the bonuses of the goal to the AP[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Inactivate another goal[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Remove another goal[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Restore another goal[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activate a goal if all the goals in a goal group are now ACTIVE[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activate a group of goals[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Inactivate a group of goals[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Remove a group of goals[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Restore a group of goals[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Display team's scores and End the Level[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mActivation[m
[32m+[m[32m----------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoals can be activated in one of the following ways:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Touched by a player[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Touched by a detpack explosion[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activated by another Goal[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activated by a Goal Group command from another Goal[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activated by a Quake Trigger[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAdditionally, the AP's details can be checked.[m
[32m+[m[32mThis allows you to have goals that are only activated if:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- The AP is of a particular class[m
[32m+[m	[32m- The AP has a particular GoalItem[m
[32m+[m	[32m- The AP is of a particular team[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGoals can also be activated only if the AP details _don't_[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mmeet the criteria specified.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mInactivation[m
[32m+[m[32m------------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoals can be inactivated in one of the following ways:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Inactivated after being ACTIVE for a specified time[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Inactivated by another Goal[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Inactivated by a Goal Group command from another Goal[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAlso, some goals are marked as Multiple Goals. They return to INACTIVE[m
[32m+[m[32mstate immediately after they become ACTIVE.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRemoval[m
[32m+[m[32m-------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoals can be removed in one of the following ways:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Removed after being activated[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Removed by another Goal[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Removed by a Goal Group command from another Goal[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Removed by a Quake Trigger[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRestoration[m
[32m+[m[32m-----------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoals can be restored in one of the following ways:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Restored by a GoalItem when it Returns (See below).[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Restored by another Goal[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Restored by a Goal Group command from another Goal[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoalItems[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoalItems are items that players can carry around.[m
[32m+[m[32mGoalItems can be placed directly into a map, where a player[m
[32m+[m[32mcan collect them as usual.[m
[32m+[m[32mAlso, on activation, Goals can give/remove GoalItems from the AP.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe details of players attempting to collect the GoalItems can[m
[32m+[m[32malso be checked.[m
[32m+[m[32mThis allows you to have GoalItems that can only be picked up if:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- The Player is of a particular class[m
[32m+[m	[32m- The Player has a particular GoalItem[m
[32m+[m	[32m- The Player is of a particular team[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGoalItems can also be set to only be picked up by players who[m
[32m+[m[32mmeet the AP criteria.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGoalItems can be returned to their starting position in any of the[m
[32m+[m[32mfollowing circumstances:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- When it's dropped by a dying player[m
[32m+[m	[32m- When it's removed from an AP by a Goal activation[m
[32m+[m	[32m- When it's untouched for a specified time[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGoalItems can affect players in the same way Goals can, except that[m
[32m+[m[32many modifications done by the GoalItem are permanent, until the[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mGoalItem is dropped.[m
[32m+[m[32mE.g. if a GoalItem grants invisibility to any players, they stay[m
[32m+[m[32minvisible until the GoalItem is dropped/removed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAlso, when they're picked up by a player, GoalItems can perform the[m
[32m+[m[32mfollowing actions on Goals:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activate another goal, applying the bonuses of the goal to the AP[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activate another goal, without applying the bonuses of the goal to the AP[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Inactivate another goal[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Remove another goal[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Restore another goal[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activate a group of goals[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Inactivate a group of goals[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Remove a group of goals[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Restore a group of goals[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGoalItems can also belong to Groups. GoalItems groups are kept[m
[32m+[m[32mseparate from Goal Groups. Operations on either of them do not[m
[32m+[m[32maffect the other type, even if the Group No is the same.[m
[32m+[m[32mUsing GoalItem groups, GoalItems can:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activate a goal if all the Items in a GoalItem group are being[m
[32m+[m	[32m  carried by players.[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activate a goal if all the Items in a GoalItem group are being[m
[32m+[m	[32m  carried by one particular player.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mTimer Goals[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mThere is also a special type of goal called a Timer Goal. TG's[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mhave a Timer Delay. TG's start INACTIVE, and then every Timer[m
[32m+[m[32mDelay seconds they activate, do their results, and inactivate.[m
[32m+[m[32mThey can also be forced to activate by other Goals. They cannot[m
[32m+[m[32mbe activated by player or detpack touches.[m
[32m+[m[32mN.B. When a TG goes ACTIVE, it does not have any AP, and hence[m
[32m+[m	[32m _cannot_ activate other goals, or apply modifications to[m
[32m+[m	[32m individual players.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mN.B. When a TG is forced to activate by another goal, they reset[m
[32m+[m	[32m their internal timer that decides when they are next going[m
[32m+[m	[32m to activate.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m E.g. If a TG with a setting of 5 seconds is forced to activate,[m
[32m+[m		[32m  it will reset it's  timer, and still activate 5 seconds after[m
[32m+[m		[32m  it was forced to activate.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSo, as a quick summary, TG's can have their state altered as[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32musual by other goals, and when they activate, they can:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Display a message to all players[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Alter the details of one or more players, as follows:[m
[32m+[m		[32m- Give a player extra lives (if applicable)[m
[32m+[m		[32m- Alter a player's health/ammo/armor/powerups[m
[32m+[m		[32m- Give a player a GoalItem[m
[32m+[m		[32m- Remove a player from an AP[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m		[32mThe player can be all the members of a Team, all the players[m[41m [m
[32m+[m		[32mon the map, or all the players within a specified distance from[m[41m [m
[32m+[m		[32mthe goal.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Inactivate another goal[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Remove another goal[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Restore another goal[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Inactivate a group of goals[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Remove a group of goals[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Restore a group of goals[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Display team's scores and End the Level[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mStandard Quake Triggers and TeamFortress Goals[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mQuake triggers can be linked into TF Goals and vice versa.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mWhen they are activated, a trigger can affect Goals[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32min the following ways:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activate a goal, applying the bonuses of the goal to the AP[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activate a goal, without applying the bonuses of the goal to the AP[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Inactivate another goal[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Remove another goal[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Restore another goal[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activate a group of goals[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Inactivate a group of goals[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Remove a group of goals[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Restore a group of goals[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen a Goal is activated, it can affect Quake Triggers[m
[32m+[m[32min the following ways:[m
[32m+[m[41m	[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activate Quake Trigger(s)[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Remove Quake Trigger(s)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDon't forget that Quake Triggers include Buttons, Doors,[m
[32m+[m[32mPlatforms, Health Boxes, Backpacks, Weapons, Armor, Keys, Sigils,[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mMonsters, Spikeshooters, Lights, Special Walls, and[m
[32m+[m[32mTeleporters..[m
[32m+[m[32mThe 'activation' of any of these things can affect goals[m
[32m+[m[32mif you want it to.[m
[32m+[m[32mTriggers Activate when:[m[41m [m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Collected by a player[m
[32m+[m		[32mHealth Boxes, Weapons, Armor, Keys, Sigils, Backpacks[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Touched by a player or hit by a weapon[m
[32m+[m		[32mButtons, Doors, Platforms, Special Walls,Teleporters[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Killed[m
[32m+[m		[32mMonsters[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAlso, Quake Triggers have been enhanced so that any Trigger[m
[32m+[m[32mcan be made to triggered only by a player if:[m
[32m+[m	[32m- The Player is of a particular class[m
[32m+[m	[32m- The Player has a particular GoalItem[m
[32m+[m	[32m- The Player is of a particular team[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis means that if the player does not match the criteria,[m
[32m+[m[32mthe following happens:[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Health Boxes, Weapons, Armor, Keys, Sigils, Backpacks[m
[32m+[m		[32mPlayer cannot pick them up.[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Buttons, Doors, Platforms, Special Walls,	Teleporters[m
[32m+[m		[32mPlayer cannot activate/open/use them.[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Monsters[m
[32m+[m		[32mPlayer cannot hurt them.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe result of 'Activation' of Triggers are as follows:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Health Boxes, Weapons, Armor, Keys, Sigils[m
[32m+[m		[32mBad. These items should never be activated by[m
[32m+[m		[32mGoals or Triggers. They should only be used[m
[32m+[m		[32mto activate other Goals/Triggers.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Buttons[m
[32m+[m		[32mThe button, if not already depressed, depressed[m
[32m+[m		[32mand sets off whatever it was designed to do.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Doors[m
[32m+[m		[32mIf the door is a DOOR_TOGGLE type door, it reveres it's[m[41m [m
[32m+[m		[32mcurrent state. e.g. Opens if it's closed, closes if it's open.[m
[32m+[m		[32mIt not, if it's closed, it opens.[m
[32m+[m[41m	[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Platforms[m
[32m+[m		[32mIf it has not been triggered before, it will lower. Otherwise,[m
[32m+[m		[32mit does nothing.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Special Walls[m
[32m+[m		[32mChanges it's texture.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Teleporters[m
[32m+[m		[32mDoesn't do anything.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Monsters[m
[32m+[m		[32mWakes the monster.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThese are a rough guide. You should look at the qc code which handles[m
[32m+[m[32mtrigger activation to see the details. Every Trigger that can be[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mactivated by another trigger/goal has a .use function.[m
[32m+[m[32mLook inside it to see how activations for that type of Trigger[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mare handled.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mOrder of Actions[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mYou don't really need to know the order in which the actions are applied,[m
[32m+[m[32mand they're far too complex now to describe them in any useful way. The[m
[32m+[m[32monly important thing of note is:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32mThe Group Goal alterations are applied _before_ the single goal[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32malterations. This is so you can do things like:[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32mInactivate an entire group, and then activate one goal in that group.[m
[32m+[m	[32mRemove an entire group, and then restore one goal in that group.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoal Technical Info[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoal behaviour is entirely defined by the variables of the Goal object[m
[32m+[m[32mwhen it is spawned at the start of the level. These variables are set[m
[32m+[m[32min the map file. Just add up the flags that you want and set the[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mvariable to that.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mE.g. If you want a goal that can be activated by a Player touch(1) and[m
[32m+[m	[32m a detpack explosion(2), you would set the "goal_activation" variable[m
[32m+[m	[32m to 3.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDon't worry! It's actually fairly easy :)[m
[32m+[m[32mN.B. Bit descriptions marked with (*) are dangerous, and should[m
[32m+[m	[32m be handled with care.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe variables of the Goals are handled as follows:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32mclassname 	:	"info_tfgoal"[m
[32m+[m	[32mbroadcast   :	Message broadcasted when this goal is activated, if any.[m
[32m+[m				[32m    Don't forget to put the \n at the end of it.[m
[32m+[m	[32mmessage		:	Message displayed to the activating player, if any.[m
[32m+[m				[32m    Don't forget to put the \n at the end of it.[m
[32m+[m	[32mdeathtype	:	Message broadcasted if the goal	kills the activating[m
[32m+[m					[32mplayer. It is appended to the name of the player.[m
[32m+[m					[32mE.g. deathtype = " gets killed by a goal!\n" displays[m
[32m+[m						[32m Bro gets killed by a goal![m
[32m+[m					[32mNot needed if this goal doesn't do damage to a player.[m
[32m+[m					[32mDon't forget to put the \n at the end of it.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32mtarget		:	If set, any Quake Triggers with the same name as this[m
[32m+[m					[32mwill be activated.[m
[32m+[m	[32mkilltarget	:	If set, any Quake Triggers with the same name as this[m
[32m+[m					[32mwill be removed.[m
[32m+[m	[32mcount		:	Score the team of the player who activates this goal gets.[m
[32m+[m					[32mUse negative numbers for penalty goals.[m
[32m+[m	[32mgoal_no		:	A unique number ID identifying this goal. Used to make[m
[32m+[m					[32mreferences to this goal in other goals.[m
[32m+[m	[32mgroup_no	:	The number of the goal group this goal belongs to.[m
[32m+[m	[32mnetname		:	This isn't used in Quake, but in the TeamFortress[m[41m [m
[32m+[m					[32mEntity Editor, it's used as the name for this goal.[m
[32m+[m	[32mnoise		:	A .wav file played when the goal is activated.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m					[32mMake sure it's a .wav file you've got. It's probably[m[41m [m
[32m+[m					[32mbest to use one of Quake's .wavs.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m					[32mIf unspecified, no sound is played.[m
[32m+[m	[32mmdl			:	The .mdl file used for this item. Make sure it's a .mdl[m
[32m+[m					[32mfile you've got. It's probably best to use one of Quake's[m
[32m+[m					[32m.mdls. If unspecified, the Goal is invisible.[m
[32m+[m[41m	[m
[32m+[m[32mAll the following attributes are applied to the attributes of[m
[32m+[m[32mevery player specified by the "goal_effect"(see below).[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m(e.g. the self.health is added to the health of the player)[m
[32m+[m	[32mlives		 :	Use negative values to remove lives from the player[m
[32m+[m	[32mhealth		 :	Use negative values to hurt the player[m
[32m+[m	[32marmortype	 : 	The player's armortype is set to this value[m
[32m+[m	[32marmorvalue	 :	The player's armorvalue is set to this value[m
[32m+[m[41m [m				[32m    Armortypes are:[m[41m   [m
[32m+[m						[32m0.3 : Green[m
[32m+[m						[32m0.6 : Yellow[m
[32m+[m						[32m0.8 : Red[m
[32m+[m	[32marmorclass	 :	The type of armor the player gets. (See Armor Types above)[m
[32m+[m	[32mfrags		 :	Use negative values to lower frag count[m
[32m+[m	[32mammo_shells  :	Use negative values to remove ammo[m
[32m+[m	[32mammo_nails   :	Use negative values to remove ammo[m
[32m+[m	[32mammo_rockets : 	Use negative values to remove ammo[m
[32m+[m	[32mammo_cells   :	Use negative values to remove ammo[m
[32m+[m	[32mammo_medikit :	Use negative values to remove ammo[m
[32m+[m	[32mammo_detpack :	Use negative values to remove ammo[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mNote A:	After applying all these values to the player, the playerclass[m[41m [m
[32m+[m		[32mlimitations of the player are applied. So if you set the health of[m[41m [m
[32m+[m		[32mthe player over that allowed, by his/her playerclass, it will then[m[41m [m
[32m+[m		[32mbe lowered to the max_health for that playerclass.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mNote B: "lives" allows you to give/remove lives from players. This is only[m
[32m+[m		[32museful if the current map limits the number of lives each player[m
[32m+[m		[32mhas. See the Auto Detection section above.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTeamFortress Grenades can be given/removed to/from the player by setting[m
[32m+[m[32mthe following two variables.[m
[32m+[m	[32mno_grenades_1	:	Use negative values to remove grenades[m
[32m+[m	[32mno_grenades_2	:	Use negative values to remove grenades[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAnd finally, the following attributes are added to the global time[m
[32m+[m[32mand applied to every player specified by the "goal_effect"(see below).[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m(e.g. if the goal's invincible_finished is 5, then the player will[m
[32m+[m[32mget invincibility for 5 seconds after activating the goal.)[m
[32m+[m	[32minvincible_finished		:	Pentagram of Protection[m[41m 	[m
[32m+[m	[32minvisible_finished		:	Ring of Shadows[m
[32m+[m	[32msuper_damage_finished	:	Quad Damage[m
[32m+[m	[32mradsuit_finished		:	Environmental Suit[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoal Activation[m
[32m+[m[32m---------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mThe "goal_activation" of the goals determine how the goal is activated.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mThe bitfields are as follows:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mActivation Details[m
[32m+[m	[32m1	:	Activated when touched by a player.[m
[32m+[m	[32m2	:	Activated when touched by a detpack explosion.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAP Details[m
[32m+[m	[32m-   If the "items_allowed" variable is non-zero, the AP must be[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m        carrying a GoalItem with an ID of "items_allowed".[m
[32m+[m[32m    -   If the "playerclass" variable is non-zero, the AP must be[m
[32m+[m[32m        be of the same class specified in "playerclass".[m
[32m+[m[32m        Classes are:[m
[32m+[m[32m            Scout             : 1[m
[32m+[m[32m            Sniper            : 2[m
[32m+[m[32m            Soldier           : 3[m
[32m+[m[32m            Demolitions Man   : 4[m
[32m+[m[32m            Medic             : 5[m
[32m+[m[32m            Heavy Weapons Guy : 6[m
[32m+[m[32m    -   If the "team_no" variable is non-zero, the AP must belong[m
[32m+[m[32m        to the same team as the number specified in "team_no".[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m4	:   This goal is only activated if the AP details above are _not_ met.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    2048:   If this bit is set, the Goal/Item drops to the ground when it[m
[32m+[m[32m            first spawns.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoal Effects[m
[32m+[m[32m---------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mThe "goal_effects" of the goal defines which players are affected by[m
[32m+[m[32mthe activation of the goal. It defaults to 1, so that only the AP is[m
[32m+[m[32maffected.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mThe player modifications of this Goal are applied to every player[m
[32m+[m[32mthat matches these criteria. GoalItems will also be given/removed[m
[32m+[m[32mto/from every one of the players matching the criteria.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe bitfields are as follows:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBasics[m
[32m+[m	[32m1	:	The AP is affected[m
[32m+[m	[32m2	:	Everyone on the AP's team is affected[m
[32m+[m	[32m4	:	Everyone not on the AP's team is affected[m
[32m+[m	[32m8	:	Everyone except the AP is affected[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSpecific Groups[m
[32m+[m	[32m- If the "maxammo_shells" variable is non-zero, then all members of that[m
[32m+[m	[32m  team are affected.[m
[32m+[m	[32m- If the "maxammo_nails" variable is non-zero, then all members of any[m
[32m+[m	[32m  team except that one are affected.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRadius[m
[32m+[m	[32m- If the "t_length" variable is non-zero, then everyone within[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m  "t_length" distance of the goal is affected, unless the above[m
[32m+[m	[32m  bitfields are in use.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  If they are, then the bitfield check is applied only to those[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m  caught in the radius.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  E.g. if "t_length" is 50, and "goal_effects" is 4, then everyone[m
[32m+[m	[32m  within 50 who isn't on the AP's team is affected.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m16	:	If set, the radius effect is obstructed by walls.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[41m  [m	[32m32	:	If a player who fits one of the other "goal_effects" variables[m
[32m+[m			[32mis not in the same environment as the Goal, don't affect him.[m
[32m+[m			[32mEnvironments are air, water, slime, lava.[m
[32m+[m			[32me.g. If a Goal is above some water, and does a radius effect[m
[32m+[m			[32m     with "t_length", and a player in the water is within the[m
[32m+[m				[32m radius, he won't be affected if this bit is set.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mNote A: If the Goal gives out a GoalItem, then every player who matches[m
[32m+[m		[32mthis criteria will get the GoalItem. This can result in lots of these[m
[32m+[m		[32mGoalItems, so be careful.[m
[32m+[m[41m		[m
[32m+[m[32m---------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoal Results[m
[32m+[m[32m---------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mThe "goal_result" of the goals determine how the goal behaves when it is[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mactivated, and the results of it's activation. It also determines what it[m
[32m+[m[32mwill do to any players that match it's "goal_effects" criteria.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe bitfields are as follows:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRespawn behaviour[m
[32m+[m	[32m1   :	The goal is immediately removed after it is activated.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "wait" variable is non-zero, then the Goal stays ACTIVE for[m
[32m+[m[32m      the "wait" seconds, and then inactivates.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  If "wait" is -1, the Goal stays active permanently.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGoalItem behaviour[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "items" variable is non-zero, the Goal gives a GoalItem[m
[32m+[m[32m      to the player. The GoalItem it gives is the Item with a GoalNo[m
[32m+[m[32m      of "items".[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "axhitme" variable is non-zero, the Goal removes a GoalItem[m
[32m+[m[32m      from the player. The GoalItem it removes is the Item with a GoalNo[m
[32m+[m[32m      of "axhitme".[m
[32m+[m[32m      If the player does not have the GoalItem, nothing happens.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGoal behaviour[m
[32m+[m	[32m2   :   If this is set, the goals activated by this one apply[m
[32m+[m[32m            their AP modifications. Otherwise, they don't.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "activate_goal_no" variable is non-zero, then the Goal with[m
[32m+[m[32m      a Goal_No equal to the variable is activated.[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "inactivate_goal_no" variable is non-zero, then the Goal with[m
[32m+[m[32m      a Goal_No equal to the variable is inactivated.[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "remove_goal_no" variable is non-zero, then the Goal with[m
[32m+[m[32m      a Goal_No equal to the variable is removed.[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "restore_goal_no" variable is non-zero, then the Goal with[m
[32m+[m[32m      a Goal_No equal to the variable is restored.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMiscellaneous[m
[32m+[m	[32m4   :	Display teamscores, fire intermission, and end the level[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m8	:	GoalItems given out by this Goal don't apply their results.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m16	:	If the player these results are being applied to is a Spy,[m
[32m+[m			[32mreset his/her skin and color.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----[m
[32m+[m[32mNote A: If (1) is not set and their is no "wait" specified, then the[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m        goal is a Multiple Goal.[m
[32m+[m		[32mAfter it activates, it will automatically inactivate.[m
[32m+[m		[32mThis is not always a good idea. When a player runs over an entity,[m
[32m+[m		[32mthe touch function will usually be run about 6 or 7 times, so the[m
[32m+[m		[32mplayer will activate the goal multiple times. If you want a player[m
[32m+[m		[32mto be able to activate it over and over again, make it respawn[m[41m [m
[32m+[m		[32mevery 2-3 seconds.[m
[32m+[m		[32mThis is especially dangerous if the goal gives out an item on[m
[32m+[m		[32mactivation, since you will end up with a _lot_ of items.[m
[32m+[m		[32mOf course, you may want this for a goal that is activated remotely[m
[32m+[m		[32mby another goal at certain times.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mNote B:	When a goal is activated by another goal, _no_ checking is done[m
[32m+[m		[32mbased on the "goal_activation" variable of the target goal. It is[m
[32m+[m		[32msimply activated. The AP who activated the original goal is used[m
[32m+[m		[32mas the activator for all the goals, but the stats of an activated[m
[32m+[m		[32mgoal are only added to the player's if (2) is set on the goal[m
[32m+[m[32m        that activates it.[m
[32m+[m		[32mGoalItems are always given/removed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoal Groups[m
[32m+[m[32m---------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoal groups allow you to do operations of multiple goals in one go.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe "group_no" of a Goal defines the ID of goal group it is in.[m
[32m+[m[32mAny goal group operation affects all goals with the specified ID.[m
[32m+[m[32mA goal's "goal_group" specifies what operations, if any, it performs[m
[32m+[m[32mon any goal groups.[m
[32m+[m[32mSince I've cleaned up the goal group handling to get rid of bitflags[m
[32m+[m[32mwhich aren't needed, there are no bits used in the "goal_group"[m
[32m+[m[32mvariable anymore :)[m
[32m+[m[32mI've left it in anyway, since some may come along later.[m
[32m+[m[32mGoal Group handling is as follows:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "all_active" variable is non-zero, then when this goal is activated,[m
[32m+[m[32m      a check is done. If all the goals in the group specified in the "all_active"[m
[32m+[m[32m      variable are ACTIVE, activate a goal with a goal number equal to the[m
[32m+[m[32m      value of the "last_impulse" variable.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "activate_group_no" variable is non-zero, activate all the[m
[32m+[m[32m      goals in that Group.[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "inactivate_group_no" variable is non-zero, inactivate all the[m
[32m+[m[32m      goals in that Group.[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "remove_group_no" variable is non-zero, remove all the[m
[32m+[m[32m      goals in that Group.[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "restore_group_no" variable is non-zero, restore all the[m
[32m+[m[32m      goals in that Group.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----[m
[32m+[m[32mNote A: When a goal is activated by another goal, _no_ checking is done[m
[32m+[m[32m        based on the "goal_activation" variable of the target goal. It is[m
[32m+[m		[32msimply activated. The AP who activated the original goal is used[m
[32m+[m		[32mas the activator for all the group goals.[m
[32m+[m		[32mBonuses of goals in groups are _never_ applied to the activating player.[m
[32m+[m		[32mGoalItems are always given/removed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mTimer Goal Technical Info[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mTimer Goals are basically identical to Goals, except they are never activated[m
[32m+[m[32mby players or detpack explosions. They automatically activate every[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m"search_time" seconds. They can also be activated by other goals and triggers.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe variables of Timer Goals are the same as Goals, except for:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32mclassname	:	"info_tfgoal_timer"[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32msearch_time :	The time in seconds that this goal activates.[m
[32m+[m					[32me.g. a search_time of 2 makes this goal activate every[m
[32m+[m						[32m 2 seconds.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAs a result of their method of activation, Timer Goals can _never_ do[m
[32m+[m[32manything that requires an AP, and they can't activate any other Goals.[m
[32m+[m[32mThey _can_ do operations on groups of players, such as all the players[m
[32m+[m[32mon the map, or all the players in a team, etc.[m
[32m+[m[32mThis is done using the "goal_effect" variable in much the same way[m
[32m+[m[32mas Goals, as follows:[m
[32m+[m[32mBasics[m
[32m+[m	[32m1	:	Illegal for Timer Goals.[m
[32m+[m	[32m2	:	Illegal for Timer Goals.[m
[32m+[m	[32m4	:	Illegal for Timer Goals.[m
[32m+[m	[32m8	:	Illegal for Timer Goals.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSpecific Groups[m
[32m+[m	[32m- If the "maxammo_shells" variable is non-zero, then all members of that[m
[32m+[m	[32m  team are affected.[m
[32m+[m	[32m- If the "maxammo_nails" variable is non-zero, then all members of any[m
[32m+[m	[32m  team except that one are affected.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRadius[m
[32m+[m	[32m- If the "t_length" variable is non-zero, then everyone within[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m  "t_length" distance of the goal is affected, unless the above[m
[32m+[m	[32m  bitfields are in use.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  If they are, then the bitfield check is applied only to those[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m  caught in the radius.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  E.g. if "t_length" is 50, and "goal_effects" is 4, then everyone[m
[32m+[m	[32m  within 50 who isn't on the AP's team is affected.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m16	:	If set, the radius effect is obstructed by walls.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[41m  [m	[32m32	:	If a player who fits one of the other "goal_effects" variables[m
[32m+[m			[32mis not in the same environment as the Goal, don't affect him.[m
[32m+[m			[32mEnvironments are air, water, slime, lava.[m
[32m+[m			[32me.g. If a Goal is above some water, and does a radius effect[m
[32m+[m			[32m     with "t_length", and a player in the water is within the[m
[32m+[m				[32m radius, he won't be affected if this bit is set.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[41m  [m	[32m64 :	If this bit is set, then instead of just applying this Goal's[m
[32m+[m			[32mresults to the group of players specified by the other[m[41m [m
[32m+[m			[32m"goal_effects" variable, this Goal checks it's criteria for[m
[32m+[m			[32meach player in the group and then applies it's results invididually[m[41m [m
[32m+[m			[32mto any of them that pass.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mNote A : The first 4 bits in the "goal_effects" are illegal for Timer Goals,[m
[32m+[m		[32m and should _never_ be set, because they involve an AP.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoal Items Technical Info[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mGoalItems do not have to be given to a player by a Goal activation.[m
[32m+[m[32mThey can be placed directly into a map.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe variables of the GoalItems are as follows:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32mclassname 	:	"item_tfgoal"[m
[32m+[m	[32mnetname  	:	Name of this GoalItem.[m
[32m+[m	[32mbroadcast	:	Message broadcasted when this goalitem is retrieved, if any.[m
[32m+[m				[32m    Don't forget to put the \n at the end of it.[m
[32m+[m	[32mmessage		:	Message displayed to a player when they get the Item, if any.[m
[32m+[m				[32m    Don't forget to put the \n at the end of it.[m
[32m+[m	[32mnoise		:	A .wav file played when the item is collected.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m					[32mMake sure it's a .wav file you've got. It's probably[m[41m [m
[32m+[m					[32mbest to use one of Quake's .wavs.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m					[32mIf unspecified, no sound is played.[m
[32m+[m	[32mmdl			:	The .mdl file used for this item. Make sure it's a .mdl[m
[32m+[m					[32mfile you've got. It's probably best to use one of Quake's[m
[32m+[m					[32m.mdls. It defaults to the silver key.[m
[32m+[m	[32mgoal_no		:	A unique number identifying this GoalItem. Used to make[m
[32m+[m					[32mreferences to this Item in goals.[m
[32m+[m[32m    goal_group  :   The number of the goalitem group this goal belongs to.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGoalItems can also modify player details in the same Goals can, using[m
[32m+[m[32mthe "goal_effects" variable (see above).[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mThe tricky bit is that any Player Modifications done by goals are added[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mwhen the player first picks the item up, and are _removed_ when the player[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mloses the item.[m
[32m+[m[32mE.g. If the item has a health of 40, then the player gets 40 health[m
[32m+[m[32m     added to their health when he/she picks it up. Then, when they[m
[32m+[m[32m     drop it, he/she loses 40 health.[m
[32m+[m[32mThere are two exceptions to this:[m[41m [m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m1.	Power-Ups. Items give the players a powerup for the entire time the[m[41m [m
[32m+[m		[32mplayer has the item. The time specified in the _finished variable[m[41m [m
[32m+[m		[32mis ignored: If it's non-zero, then all players the GoalItem specifies[m
[32m+[m		[32mget the power-up while item is still carried.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m2.  GoalItems. Items given/removed by another GoalItem when it's picked up[m
[32m+[m		[32mare not removed/given back when the original GoalItem is dropped/removed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWith the "goal_effects" variable you can make Items affect more than[m
[32m+[m[32mone player. This is done exactly as if it was just one person.[m
[32m+[m[32mE.g. If the Item adds health to everyone, then as soon as any player[m
[32m+[m[32mpicks it up, the modifications are applied to everyone, and as soon as[m
[32m+[m[32mit's dropped, the modifications are removed from everyone.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAlso, GoalItems can affect Goals in much the same way as other Goals,[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mas follows:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "activate_goal_no" variable is non-zero, then the Goal with[m
[32m+[m[32m      a Goal_No equal to the variable is activated.[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "inactivate_goal_no" variable is non-zero, then the Goal with[m
[32m+[m[32m      a Goal_No equal to the variable is inactivated.[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "remove_goal_no" variable is non-zero, then the Goal with[m
[32m+[m[32m      a Goal_No equal to the variable is removed.[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "restore_goal_no" variable is non-zero, then the Goal with[m
[32m+[m[32m      a Goal_No equal to the variable is restored.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "activate_group_no" variable is non-zero, activate all the[m
[32m+[m[32m      goals in that Group.[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "inactivate_group_no" variable is non-zero, inactivate all the[m
[32m+[m[32m      goals in that Group.[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "remove_group_no" variable is non-zero, remove all the[m
[32m+[m[32m      goals in that Group.[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "restore_group_no" variable is non-zero, restore all the[m
[32m+[m[32m      goals in that Group.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGoalItems can use the "goal_result" variable. The Bitfields are as follows:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m2	:	Goals activated by this Item don't apply bonuses to the AP.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m16	:	If the player these results are being applied to is a Spy,[m
[32m+[m			[32mreset his/her skin and color.[m
[32m+[m			[32mWhen a Spy is carrying a GoalItem with this bit set, he/she[m
[32m+[m			[32mwill be unable to change skin and color.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen Goals are activated by a GoalItem, the AP used to activate the Goals[m
[32m+[m[32mis the Player who picked up the Item. AP Modifications are applied if (512)[m
[32m+[m[32mis set it the "goal_activation" variable (see below).[m
[32m+[m[32mGoalItems themselves have various bitfields to depict the GoalItem's[m
[32m+[m[32mbehaviour. The bitfields are stored in the GoalItem's "goal_activation"[m
[32m+[m[32mvariable, and are:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCarrying Details[m
[32m+[m[32m    1	:   Any player carrying this item will glow.[m
[32m+[m[32m    2	:   Any player carrying this item will move at half-speed.[m
[32m+[m[32m(*) 4	:   When a player carrying this is killed, the item will be dropped[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mReturning[m
[32m+[m[32m    8	:   Return the item if dropped by a dying player[m
[32m+[m[32m    16	:   Return the item if removed from a player by a goal activation.[m
[32m+[m[32m    32	:   Return the item if removed from the map by the action of the[m
[32m+[m[32m            (128) (see below).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "impulse" variable is non-zero, then when the GoalItem[m
[32m+[m[32m      is returned by one of the above, the goal with a Goal No equal to[m
[32m+[m[32m      the "impulse" is restored.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPickup Details[m
[32m+[m[32m     - If the "items_allowed" variable is non-zero, the Player must be[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m       carrying a GoalItem with an ID matching the variable. If not,[m
[32m+[m[32m       he/she will not be able to get this item.[m
[32m+[m[32m     - If the "playerclass" variable is non-zero, the Player must be[m
[32m+[m[32m       be of the same class specified in the variable. If not,[m
[32m+[m[32m       he/she will not be able to get this item.[m
[32m+[m[32m       Classes are:[m
[32m+[m[32m             Scout             : 1[m
[32m+[m[32m             Sniper            : 2[m
[32m+[m[32m             Soldier           : 3[m
[32m+[m[32m             Demolitions Man   : 4[m
[32m+[m[32m             Medic             : 5[m
[32m+[m[32m             Heavy Weapons Guy : 6[m
[32m+[m[32m     - If the "team_no" variable is non-zero, the Player must belong[m
[32m+[m[32m       to the same team as the number specified in the variable.[m
[32m+[m[32m       If not, he/she will not be able to get this item.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m64	:	This GoalItem can only be picked up by a player if they _don't_[m
[32m+[m			[32mmatch the player details above.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMiscellaneous[m
[32m+[m[32m    128 :   If this is set, then, after the goal is dropped by a player,[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m            if it has not been touched for the time specified in the[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m            "pausetime" variable, in seconds, it is removed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "distance" variable is non-zero, then, If all GoalItems in the[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m      goalitem group specified by "distance" are being carried by players,[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m      activate a goal, the Goal No of which is specified in "pain_finished".[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "speed" variable is non-zero, then, If all GoalItems in the[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m      goalitem group specified by "speed" are being carried by one player,[m
[32m+[m[32m      activate a goal, the Goal No of which is specified in "attack_finished".[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m256 :	If a player carrying this Item dies, they keep it, even after[m
[32m+[m			[32mthey respawn.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m512 :   If this Item is not being carried by a goal, it glows.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m1024: 	When this item is removed from a player, don't remove the[m[41m [m
[32m+[m			[32meffects this item gave the player.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    2048: If this bit is set, the Goal/Item drops to the ground when it[m
[32m+[m[32m          first spawns.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    4096: If this bit is set, any player carrying this item can drop[m
[32m+[m[32m          it using the "dropitems" command.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----[m
[32m+[m[32mNote A: (4) is dangerous. If you have goals giving out this item multiple[m
[32m+[m[32m        times, make sure the item is getting removed somehow, or you could[m
[32m+[m[32m        end up with too many items on the map.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mNote B: The Pickup Details are only used when a player picks up this[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m        item directly. If this item is given to an AP by a goal, these[m
[32m+[m[32m        are ignored.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mNote D: (128) allows you to make items that are untouched for a while[m[41m [m
[32m+[m		[32mdisappear. This should be set if you have Goals that give out[m[41m [m
[32m+[m		[32mmultiple copies of GoalItems that are dropped when players[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m    carrying them are killed. Otherwise you could end up with too many[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m    entities on the map :)[m
[32m+[m	[32m    If you have a GoalItem that is only given out once and is dropped[m
[32m+[m	[32m    when players with it die, you will probably want to set (128)[m
[32m+[m	[32m    and (32), so that if it falls in lava or something, it'll be[m[41m [m
[32m+[m		[32mreturned.[m
[32m+[m	[32m    If you don't specify a value, "pausetime" defaults to 2 minutes.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mQuake Triggers that use TeamFortress Goals Technical Details[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mFor Triggers to use Goals, you need to use various variables.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mTriggers can use the same AP criteria matching as Goals, as follows:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m-   If the "items_allowed" variable is non-zero, the AP must be[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m        carrying a GoalItem with an ID of "items_allowed".[m
[32m+[m[32m    -   If the "playerclass" variable is non-zero, the AP must be[m
[32m+[m[32m        be of the same class specified in "playerclass".[m
[32m+[m[32m        Classes are:[m
[32m+[m[32m            Scout             : 1[m
[32m+[m[32m            Sniper            : 2[m
[32m+[m[32m            Soldier           : 3[m
[32m+[m[32m            Demolitions Man   : 4[m
[32m+[m[32m            Medic             : 5[m
[32m+[m[32m            Heavy Weapons Guy : 6[m
[32m+[m[32m    -   If the "team_no" variable is non-zero, the AP must belong[m
[32m+[m[32m        to the same team as the number specified in "team_no".[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf any of the following variables is not set, or 0, then the effect of that[m
[32m+[m[32mvariable is simply not used.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe variables are:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32mactivate_goal_no	:	Activates a goal with a goal_no equal to this.[m
[32m+[m	[32minactivate_goal_no	:	Inactivates a goal with a goal_no equal to this.[m
[32m+[m	[32mremove_goal_no		:	Removes a goal with a goal_no equal to this.[m
[32m+[m	[32mrestore_goal_no		:	Restores a goal with a goal_no equal to this.[m
[32m+[m[41m								   [m
[32m+[m	[32mactivate_group_no	:	Activates a group of goals with a goal_group equal to this.[m
[32m+[m	[32minactivate_group_no	:	Inactivates a group of goals with a goal_group equal to this.[m
[32m+[m	[32mremove_group_no		:	Removes a group of goals with a goal_group equal to this.[m
[32m+[m	[32mrestore_group_no	:	Restores a group of goals with a goal_group equal to this.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAlso:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- If the "goal_result" variable of the Trigger is 0, then any Goals[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m  activated by this Trigger _don't_ add bonuses to the AP. If it's 2, they do.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    - If the "all_active" variable is non-zero, then when this Trigger is activated,[m
[32m+[m[32m      a check is done. If all the goals in the group specified in the "all_active"[m
[32m+[m[32m      variable are ACTIVE, activate a goal with a goal number equal to the[m
[32m+[m[32m      value of the "last_impulse" variable.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIn all cases, the AP for the goals will be set to the "activator". If the[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mAP is not a player, then no player-related operations will be performed by[m
[32m+[m[32mthe Goals, or any Goals activated by those Goals.[m
[32m+[m[32mThis stuff is kind of dangerous, if the Trigger isn't activated by a player,[m
[32m+[m[32mand the Goals your playing with alter other Goals. Just be careful :)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mSummary of Changes[m
[32m+[m[32m----------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32mThis is a summary of changes in the map specs from TeamFortress v1.3x[m
[32m+[m[32mto TeamFortress v2.x :[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- All entities, most especially GoalItems, can specify the team[m
[32m+[m	[32m  they belong to by putting the team number in the "owned_by" variable.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- The "goal_state" variable allows you to set the starting state[m
[32m+[m	[32m  of a goal. The available states are:[m
[32m+[m			[32mActive 	 				1[m[41m [m
[32m+[m			[32mInactive (default) 		2[m[41m [m
[32m+[m			[32mRemoved					3[m[41m [m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Activation criteria for Goals/Items/Timers/Triggers can[m
[32m+[m	[32m  now include the Checking of the state of other Goals[m
[32m+[m	[32m  The following variables are used:[m
[32m+[m	[32m   "if_goal_is_active"   : If this is non-zero, the goal will only activate[m
[32m+[m							[32m   if the goal with a "goal_no" matching[m[41m [m
[32m+[m							[32m   "if_goal_is_active" is active.[m
[32m+[m	[32m   "if_goal_is_inactive" : As above, if the goal is inactive.[m
[32m+[m	[32m   "if_goal_is_removed"  : As above, if the goal is removed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m   "if_group_is_active"  : As above, except that all goals with a "group_no"[m
[32m+[m							[32m   matching "if_group_is_active" must be active.[m
[32m+[m	[32m   "if_group_is_inactive": As above, if all the group is inactive.[m
[32m+[m	[32m   "if_group_is_removed" : As above, if all the group is removed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Upon activation, Goals can now centerprint more intelligently,[m
[32m+[m	[32m  as follows:[m
[32m+[m		[32m"broadcast"			 : Instead of being bprinted, it now gets[m
[32m+[m							[32m   centerprinted to everyone, except the AP.[m
[32m+[m							[32m   You'll probably want to use "team_broadcast"[m
[32m+[m							[32m   and "non_team_broadcast" instead.[m
[32m+[m		[32m"message"			 : Instead of sprinting to the AP, it now[m
[32m+[m							[32m   centerprints.[m
[32m+[m		[32m"team_broadcast"	 : Gets centerprinted to all of the AP's team,[m
[32m+[m							[32m   except the AP.[m
[32m+[m		[32m"non_team_broadcast" : Gets centerprinted to all non-AP-teammembers.[m
[32m+[m							[32m   If there is a "owners_team_broadcast" specified,[m
[32m+[m							[32m   it isn't centerprinted to members of the team[m
[32m+[m							[32m   that own the goal/item.[m
[32m+[m		[32m"owners_team_broadcast" : Gets centerprinted to all the members of the[m
[32m+[m							[32m      team that own the goal/item.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- The detection entity can now supply the Team Menu string, which[m
[32m+[m	[32m  effectively allows you to provide names for team.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  The string should be put in the detection entity's "team_broadcast" var.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  It gets centerprinted when player's are asked to join a team,[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m  so it should be similar to the following format:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m		[32m"=== Choose your team ===\n\n1.. Team One  \n\n\n\n\n7.. Bind my keys for me!\n\nFor full details on this patch:\nhttp://yallara.cs.rmit.edu.au/~cookj\n"[m
[32m+[m		[32m"=== Choose your team ===\n\n2.. Team One  \n2.. Team Two  \n\n\n\n\n7.. Bind my keys for me!\n\nFor full details on this patch:\nhttp://yallara.cs.rmit.edu.au/~cookj\n"[m
[32m+[m		[32m"=== Choose your team ===\n\n2.. Team One  \n2.. Team Two  \n3.. Team Three\n\n\n\n\n7.. Bind my keys for me!\n\nFor full details on this patch:\nhttp://yallara.cs.rmit.edu.au/~cookj\n"[m
[32m+[m		[32m"=== Choose your team ===\n\n3.. Team One  \n2.. Team Two  \n3.. Team Three\n4.. Team Four \n\n\n\n\n7.. Bind my keys for me!\n\nFor full details on this patch:\nhttp://yallara.cs.rmit.edu.au/~cookj\n"[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m  Other examples are:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32m"=== Choose your team ===\n\n1.. Blue Team \n2.. Red Team  \n\n\n\n7.. Bind keys"[m
[32m+[m		[32m"=== Choose your team ===\n\n1.. Attackers \n2.. Defenders \n\n\n\n7.. Bind keys"[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m  You need to have a team number and choice for every team on your map.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  Don't forget that TF determines the number of teams on a map based upon[m
[32m+[m	[32m  the Teamspawn points. If there are spawn points for 3 teams, then you[m
[32m+[m	[32m  should have three teams in the team menu string.[m
[32m+[m[41m	[m
[32m+[m	[32m  N.B. Unfortunately, qbsp prevents you from having large strings, so you[m
[32m+[m	[32m       have to be curt. If you get a "Token too large" error when qbsping,[m
[32m+[m		[32m   then you've got the string too long.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- The detection entity can now specify a Map Help string in it's[m
[32m+[m	[32m  "non_team_broadcast" variable.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  Player's can do the Map Help impulse, and the Map Help string will[m
[32m+[m	[32m  be printed. The string can be anything you like, but it should be[m
[32m+[m	[32m  a quick description of the goal of the map, such as:[m
[32m+[m[41m  [m		[32m"Havoc: Get into the enemy's castle and destroy their computer room!\n"[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m  End the string with a \n.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  N.B. Unfortunately, qbsp prevents you from having large strings, so you[m
[32m+[m	[32m       have to be curt. If you get a "Token too large" error when qbsping,[m
[32m+[m		[32m   then you've got the string too long.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- All Entities can specify whether they exist for different skill[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m  settings, as follows:[m
[32m+[m		[32m"ex_skill_min" 	: The entity only exists when the skill variable[m
[32m+[m						[32m  is >= to this value.[m
[32m+[m		[32m"ex_skill_max" 	: The entity only exists when the skill variable[m
[32m+[m						[32m  is <= to this value.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m  N.B. The checking is done in the initial spawning, so if the skill[m
[32m+[m		[32m   changes during the level, it will have no effect on the entities.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m  You can use this to do so many things, such as making plats move[m
[32m+[m	[32m  in different trains at different skill levels, more/less monsters[m
[32m+[m	[32m  and ammo and different levels, more secrets at higher levels, etc.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Team Spawnpoints can set their "goal_effects" variable to 1, which[m
[32m+[m	[32m  makes them remove themselves after someone has spawned on them.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  Use this to make a team spawn inside their base initially, and then[m
[32m+[m	[32m  spawn throughout the level for the rest of the game.[m
[32m+[m[41m	[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Items now have a ItemGlow flag, which makes the Item glow when it's[m
[32m+[m	[32m  not being carried by a player.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  The flag is Bit 10 (512) in the Goalitem's "goal_activation" variable.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- The Detection entity can now restrict the classes available to[m
[32m+[m	[32m  members of particular teams, in the following variables:[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 1	:	"maxammo_shells"[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 2	:	"maxammo_nails"[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 3	:	"maxammo_rockets"[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 4	:	"maxammo_cells"[m
[32m+[m[41m	[m
[32m+[m	[32m- The Detection entity can now specify a Class Selection string for[m
[32m+[m	[32m  any team. The default string allows them to pick any class, but you[m
[32m+[m	[32m  may want to refine it for teams that have a limited selection of[m
[32m+[m	[32m  classes.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  If you don't supply one, the default will be used.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  The strings should be put in following Detection entity variables :[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 1 String	:	"noise1"[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 2 String	:	"noise2"[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 3 String	:	"noise3"[m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32mTeam 4 String	:	"noise4"[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m  The default string looks like this:[m
[32m+[m[41m                                                                                                                                        [m
[32m+[m		[32m"=== Choose your class ===\n\n1.. Scout   \n2.. Sniper  \n3.. Soldier \n4.. Demoman \n5.. Medic   \n6.. Hvwep   \n7.. Pyro    \n8.. Spy     \n9.. Engineer\n0.. Randompc\n"[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m  But if you restricted Team 1 to Scout, Demoman, and Medic, you might[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m  want to set the "noise1" variable to:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m		[32m"=== Choose your class ===\n\n1.. Scout   \n4.. Demoman \n5.. Medic   \n"[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m  N.B. You _MUST_ not alter the numbering of the class.[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[41m  [m	[32m   e.g. Sniper must always be selected with 2, Demoman with 4, etc.[m
[32m+[m	[32m  N.B. Unfortunately, qbsp prevents you from having large strings, so you[m
[32m+[m	[32m       have to be curt. If you get a "Token too large" error when qbsping,[m
[32m+[m		[32m   then you've got the string too long.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m	[32m- Any Goal can now specify an 'else' goal. This is a goal which attempts[m
[32m+[m	[32m  to activate if this goal fails to activate because it's Criteria[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m  wasn't met. The "goal_no" of the 'else' goal should be specified in[m[41m [m
[32m+[m	[32m  the Goal's "else_goal" variable. 'else' Goals still check their[m
[32m+[m	[32m  criteria, the AP being the player who failed the first goal's criteria.[m
[32m+[m[41m		    [m
[32m+[m	[32m- The Detection entity can now specify a maximum number of players[m
